(window.RW_DISPLAY = window.RW_DISPLAY || {})["text-structure-and-purpose_3"] = [{"id":"2d77660e","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"In the late 1800s, Spanish-language newspapers flourished in cities across Texas. San Antonio alone produced eleven newspapers in Spanish between 1890 and 1900. But El Paso surpassed all other cities in the state. This city produced twenty-two newspapers in Spanish during that period. El Paso is located on the border with Mexico and has always had a large population of Spanish speakers. Thus, it is unsurprising that this city became such a rich site for Spanish-language journalism.","question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To compare Spanish-language newspapers published in Texas today with ones published there during the late 1800s","To explain that Spanish-language newspapers thrived in Texas and especially in El Paso during the late 1800s","To argue that Spanish-language newspapers published in El Paso influenced the ones published in San Antonio during the late 1800s","To explain why Spanish-language newspapers published in Texas were so popular in Mexico during the late 1800s"]},{"id":"3e63fce0","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"A team of researchers discovered that Matabele ants can identify an infected wound in a member of the colony and then treat the infection by covering the wound with antimicrobial secretions that the ants produce. The team found that the mortality rate for Matabele ants with infected injuries was reduced by 90% with this treatment, and they are hopeful that this discovery could aid in the development of new antibiotics for human use.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"A team of researchers discovered that Matabele ants can identify an infected wound in a member of the colony and then treat the infection by","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"covering the wound with antimicrobial secretions that the ants produce. The team found that the mortality rate for Matabele ants with infected","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"injuries was reduced by 90% with this treatment, and they are hopeful that this discovery could aid in the development of new antibiotics for","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"human use.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["It summarizes research findings on Matabele ants and then identifies an area for further research.","It introduces a study of Matabele ants and then explains the research methods used in the study.","It describes unique properties of Matabele ants and then speculates on how those properties evolved.","It identifies an issue concerning Matabele ants and then proposes a solution to address the issue."]},{"id":"82cb7dda","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The field of study called affective neuroscience seeks instinctive, physiological causes for feelings such as pleasure or displeasure. Because these sensations are linked to a chemical component (for example, the release of the neurotransmitter dopamine in the brain when one receives or expects a reward), they can be said to have a partly physiological basis. These processes have been described in mammals, but Jingnan Huang and his colleagues have recently observed that some behaviors of honeybees (such as foraging) are also motivated by a dopamine-based signaling process. What choice best describes","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The field of study called affective neuroscience seeks instinctive, physiological causes for feelings such as pleasure or displeasure. Because","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"these sensations are linked to a chemical component (for example, the release of the neurotransmitter dopamine in the brain when one receives","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"or expects a reward), they can be said to have a partly physiological basis. These processes have been described in mammals, but Jingnan","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Huang and his colleagues have recently observed that some behaviors of honeybees (such as foraging) are also motivated by a dopamine-based","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"signaling process.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["It describes an experimental method of measuring the strength of physiological responses in humans.","It illustrates processes by which certain insects can express how they are feeling.","It summarizes a finding suggesting that some mechanisms in the brains of certain insects resemble mechanisms in mammalian brains.","It presents research showing that certain insects and mammals behave similarly when there is a possibility of a reward for their actions."]},{"id":"a1d2c4d0","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Hard","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Pteropods are small swimming snails with thin, delicate calcium carbonate shells. These animals are thought to be especially vulnerable to ocean acidification due to calcium carbonate’s susceptibility to dissolution at lower pH values. Victoria L. Peck and colleagues recently found that the periostracum (a protective coating on pteropods’ outer shells) prevents this dissolution when intact. Moreover, the team was surprised to discover that even when the periostracum is breached, pteropods can still mitigate damage by rebuilding the inner shell wall.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Pteropods are small swimming snails with thin, delicate calcium carbonate shells. These animals are thought to be especially vulnerable to","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"ocean acidification due to calcium carbonate’s susceptibility to dissolution at lower pH values. Victoria L. Peck and colleagues recently found","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"that the periostracum (a protective coating on pteropods’ outer shells) prevents this dissolution when intact. Moreover, the team was surprised","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"to discover that even when the periostracum is breached, pteropods can still mitigate damage by rebuilding the inner shell wall.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To call for additional research on biological mechanisms that improve pteropod survival rates","To discuss a conclusion drawn in a study of calcium carbonate’s role in protecting the periostracum of pteropods","To address some of the ways ocean acidification has altered pteropod behavior over time","To present findings that suggest that a concern about the effects of ocean acidification on pteropod shells may be unwarranted"]},{"id":"809addda","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Ameen Rihani’s 1921 poem “The Wanderer.” I wander among the hills of alien lands Where Nature her prerogative resigns To Man; where Comfort in her shack reclines And all the arts and sciences commands. But in my soul The eastern billows roll — I hear the voices of my native strands.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Ameen Rihani’s 1921 poem “The Wanderer.”","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"I wander among the hills of alien lands","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Where Nature her prerogative resigns","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"To Man; where Comfort in her shack reclines","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"And all the arts and sciences commands.","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"But in my soul","indent":3},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"The eastern billows roll—","indent":3},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"I hear the voices of my native strands.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined lines in the text as a whole?","choices":["It establishes that the speaker’s enthusiasm about current travels conflicts with the growing urge to return home.","It illustrates the speaker’s uncertainty about maintaining strong links with relatives in distant places.","It conveys the speaker’s sense of feeling a pull toward home while traveling in an unfamiliar place.","It reveals that upon returning after an extended absence, the speaker longs for the way a location once felt."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["But in my soul","The eastern billows roll—","I hear the voices of my native strands."]},{"id":"617a8a10","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Very little is known about the role nocturnal insects, such as moths, play in flower pollination because it is difficult to monitor insects at night. To address this problem, a team of scientists used time-lapse cameras to record pollinator visits to red clover all day and night. The recordings showed that while most pollinator visits were by bumblebees, one-third of visits were by moths. Additionally, flowers that were visited by both moths and bees produced more seeds than flowers that were only visited by bees.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Very little is known about the role nocturnal insects, such as moths, play in flower pollination because it is difficult to monitor insects at night. To","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"address this problem, a team of scientists used time-lapse cameras to record pollinator visits to red clover all day and night. The recordings","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"showed that while most pollinator visits were by bumblebees, one-third of visits were by moths. Additionally, flowers that were visited by both","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"moths and bees produced more seeds than flowers that were only visited by bees.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the function of the underlined sentence?","choices":["To describe an approach a team of scientists used to study pollinators","To question a claim scientists make about pollinators","To explain why moths prefer red clover to other flowers","To announce an unexpected research finding about red clover"],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["To","address this problem, a team of scientists used time-lapse cameras to record pollinator visits to red clover all day and night."]},{"id":"c6bd3447","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Virginia Woolf’s 1919 novel Night and Day. The text describes a gathering of young artists and intellectuals. One person after another rose, and, as with an ill-balanced axe, attempted to hew out his conception of art a little more clearly, and sat down with the feeling that, for some reason which he could not grasp, his strokes had gone awry. As they sat down they turned almost invariably to the person sitting next them, and rectified and continued what they had just said in public.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Virginia Woolf’s 1919 novel Night and Day. The text describes a gathering of young artists and intellectuals.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"One person after another rose, and, as with an ill-balanced axe, attempted to hew out his conception of art a little more clearly,","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"and sat down with the feeling that, for some reason which he could not grasp, his strokes had gone awry. As they sat down they","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"turned almost invariably to the person sitting next them, and rectified and continued what they had just said in public.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portions in the text as a whole?","choices":["To demonstrate individuals puzzlement over the reputation of a certain artwork","To highlight the physical effort involved in individuals construction of large-scale works of art","To draw attention to individuals discontent with the group’s conversation about art","To emphasize the extent of individuals struggles to articulate thoughts on art"],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["an ill-balanced axe, attempted to hew out","strokes had gone awry."]},{"id":"0ed94d4c","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Jackie Ormes’s Torchy Brown in Dixie to Harlem (1937 –38) was the first comic strip by a Black woman to appear in a widely read newspaper. The strip tells the story of Torchy, a young woman who leaves Mississippi to become a performer in New York City. Torchy’s story reflects the experience of the Great Migration (1910 –1970), when millions of Black Americans left the South in search of opportunities in other parts of the United States. Torchy Brown thus shows how Ormes used comics to comment humorously on issues affecting Black Americans, which she continued to do throughout her career.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Jackie Ormes’s Torchy Brown in Dixie to Harlem (1937–38) was the first comic strip by a Black woman to appear in a widely read newspaper. The","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"strip tells the story of Torchy, a young woman who leaves Mississippi to become a performer in New York City. Torchy’s story reflects the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"experience of the Great Migration (1910–1970), when millions of Black Americans left the South in search of opportunities in other parts of the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"United States. Torchy Brown thus shows how Ormes used comics to comment humorously on issues affecting Black Americans, which she","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"continued to do throughout her career.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To show how Ormes’s Torchy Brown inspired other Black women to write comic strips in the 1930s","To illustrate how the subjects Ormes addressed in her comic strips changed over the course of her career","To give an example of how Ormes presented the experiences of Black Americans in her comic strips","To claim that several characters in Torchy Brown were based on people that Ormes knew personally"]},{"id":"9c759a09","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Georgia Douglas Johnson’s 1922 poem “Benediction.” Go forth, my son, Winged by my heart’s desire! Great reaches, yet unknown, Await For your possession. I may not, if I would, Retrace the way with you, My pilgrimage is through, But life is calling you!","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Georgia Douglas Johnson’s 1922 poem “Benediction.”","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"Go forth, my son,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Winged by my heart’s desire!","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Great reaches, yet unknown,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Await","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"For your possession.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"I may not, if I would,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Retrace the way with you,","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"My pilgrimage is through,","indent":0},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"But life is calling you!","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To express hope that a child will have the same accomplishments as his parent did","To suggest that raising a child involves many struggles","To warn a child that he will face many challenges throughout his life","To encourage a child to embrace the experiences life will offer"]},{"id":"422c5068","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Generally it takes Tule geese about four days to migrate south for the winter. From their summer breeding grounds in Cook Inlet, Alaska, the birds begin by flying over the Gulf of Alaska, keeping about 100 miles from the Canadian shore. They pause to rest on the Pacific Ocean, then fly toward Summer Lake, Oregon, before finally arriving at their winter destination of Sacramento Valley, California. In 2020, however, it took the geese over twice as long to make their way from Cook Inlet to Sacramento Valley. According to researchers, the reason was airborne pollutants.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Generally it takes Tule geese about four days to migrate south for the winter. From their summer breeding grounds in Cook Inlet, Alaska, the birds","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"begin by flying over the Gulf of Alaska, keeping about 100 miles from the Canadian shore. They pause to rest on the Pacific Ocean, then fly","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"toward Summer Lake, Oregon, before finally arriving at their winter destination of Sacramento Valley, California. In 2020, however, it took the","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"geese over twice as long to make their way from Cook Inlet to Sacramento Valley. According to researchers, the reason was airborne pollutants.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?","choices":["It illustrates a change in Tule geese’s usual flight behavior.","It suggests an explanation for why Tule geese breed in Alaska.","It describes part of the Tule geese’s typical winter migration journey.","It compares Tule geese to other birds that migrate south for the winter."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["the birds","begin by flying over the Gulf of Alaska, keeping about 100 miles from the Canadian shore."]},{"id":"e7247766","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"Horizontal gene transfer occurs when an organism of one species acquires genetic material from an organism of another species through nonreproductive means. The genetic material can then be transferred “vertically” — in the second species that is, through reproductive inheritance. Scientist Atma Ivancevic and her team have hypothesized infection by invertebrate parasites as a mechanism of horizontal gene transfer between vertebrate species: while feeding, a parasite could acquire a gene from one host, then relocate to a host from a different vertebrate species and transfer the gene to it in turn.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"Horizontal gene transfer occurs when an organism of one species acquires genetic material from an organism of another species through","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"nonreproductive means. The genetic material can then be transferred “vertically” in the second species—that is, through reproductive inheritance.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Scientist Atma Ivancevic and her team have hypothesized infection by invertebrate parasites as a mechanism of horizontal gene transfer","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"between vertebrate species: while feeding, a parasite could acquire a gene from one host, then relocate to a host from a different vertebrate","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"species and transfer the gene to it in turn.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best describes the function of the underlined portion in the text as a whole?","choices":["It explains why parasites are less susceptible to horizontal gene transfer than their hosts are.","It clarifies why some genes are more likely to be transferred horizontally than others are.","It contrasts how horizontal gene transfer occurs among vertebrates with how it occurs among invertebrates.","It describes a means by which horizontal gene transfer might occur among vertebrates."],"underline":null,"underline_segments":["while feeding, a parasite could acquire a gene from one host, then relocate to a host from a different vertebrate","species and transfer the gene to it in turn."]},{"id":"f631132b","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"In the Here and Now Storybook (1921), educator Lucy Sprague Mitchell advanced the then controversial idea that books for very young children should imitate how they use language, since toddlers, who cannot yet grasp narrative or abstract ideas, seek reassurance in verbal repetition and naming. The most enduring example of this idea is Margaret Wise Brown’s 1947 picture book Goodnight Moon, in which a young rabbit names the objects in his room as he drifts off to sleep. Scholars note that the book’s emphasis on repetition, rhythm, and nonsense rhyme speaks directly to Mitchell’s influence.","question":"Which choice best describes the overall structure of the text?","choices":["The text outlines a debate between two authors of children’s literature and then traces how that debate shaped theories on early childhood education.","The text summarizes an argument about how children’s literature should be evaluated and then discusses a contrasting view on that subject.","The text lists the literary characteristics that are common to many classics of children’s literature and then indicates the narrative subjects that are most appropriate for young children.","The text presents a philosophy about what material is most suitable for children’s literature and then describes a book influenced by that philosophy."]},{"id":"ea971260","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is adapted from Louisa May Alcott’s 1869 novel An Old-Fashioned Girl. Polly, a teenager, is visiting her friend Fanny. Fanny’s friends did not interest Polly much; she was rather afraid of them [because] they seemed so much older and wiser than herself, even those younger in years. They talked about things of which she knew nothing and when Fanny tried to explain, she didn’t find them interesting; indeed, some of them rather shocked and puzzled her.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is adapted from Louisa May Alcott’s 1869 novel An Old-Fashioned Girl. Polly, a teenager, is visiting her friend Fanny.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Fanny’s friends did not interest Polly much; she was rather afraid of them [because] they seemed so much older and wiser than","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"herself, even those younger in years. They talked about things of which she knew nothing and when Fanny tried to explain, she","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"didn’t find them interesting; indeed, some of them rather shocked and puzzled her.","indent":2}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To portray Polly’s reaction to Fanny’s friends","To identify the topics Polly talks about with Fanny’s friends","To explain how Fanny met some of her friends","To illustrate how Fanny’s friends feel about Polly"]},{"id":"ae2b3112","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Medium","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"By combining Indigenous and classical music, Cree composer and cellist Cris Derksen creates works that reflect the diverse cultural landscape of Canada. For her album Orchestral Powwow, Derksen composed new songs in the style of traditional powwow music that were accompanied by classical arrangements played by an orchestra. But where an orchestra would normally follow the directions of a conductor, the musicians on Orchestral Powwow are led by the beat of a powwow drum.","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"By combining Indigenous and classical music, Cree composer and cellist Cris Derksen creates works that reflect the diverse cultural landscape","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"of Canada. For her album Orchestral Powwow, Derksen composed new songs in the style of traditional powwow music that were accompanied","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"by classical arrangements played by an orchestra. But where an orchestra would normally follow the directions of a conductor, the musicians on","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"Orchestral Powwow are led by the beat of a powwow drum.","indent":0}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["To examine how Derksen’s musical compositions blend cultures","To argue that Derksen should be recognized for creating a new style of music","To describe the difficulties Derksen encountered when producing her album","To establish a contrast between Derksen’s classical training and her Cree heritage"]},{"id":"48e4021d","domain":"Craft and Structure","skill":"Text Structure and Purpose","difficulty":"Easy","context":"Craft and Structure · Text Structure and Purpose","passage":"The following text is from Holly Goldberg Sloan’s 2017 novel Short. More than two years ago my parents bought a piano from some people who were moving to Utah. Mom and Dad gave it to my brothers and me for Christmas. I had to act really happy because it was such a big present, but I pretty much hated the thing from the second it was carried into the hallway upstairs, which is right next to my bedroom. The piano glared at me. It was like a songbird in a cage. It wanted to be set free. ©2017 by Holly Goldberg Sloan","passage_lines":[{"type":"line","text":"The following text is from Holly Goldberg Sloan’s 2017 novel Short.","indent":0},{"type":"line","text":"More than two years ago my parents bought a piano from some people who were moving to Utah. Mom and Dad gave it to my","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"brothers and me for Christmas. I had to act really happy because it was such a big present, but I pretty much hated the thing from","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"the second it was carried into the hallway upstairs, which is right next to my bedroom. The piano glared at me. It was like a","indent":2},{"type":"line","text":"songbird in a cage. It wanted to be set free.","indent":2},{"type":"blank"},{"type":"line","text":"©2017 by Holly Goldberg Sloan","indent":4}],"question":"Which choice best states the main purpose of the text?","choices":["It explains why the narrator always wanted a piano close to her bedroom.","It establishes how the narrator feels about the piano.","It suggests that the narrator’s brothers are talented piano players.","It describes the event that led the narrator’s parents to buy a piano."]}];
